    "q-161666": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161666",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2x[y]_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=2-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{32}{3}-8)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161666-a",
