    "q-40403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40403",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xyz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-2z},\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xyz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}xz[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $x$ and then with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-2z}}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(4-2z)^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =(8-\\frac{32}{3}+4)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
