    "q-161689": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161689",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}5yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-z\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ and $x$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}5yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}5z{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{∬}_{D}z(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $x$ and then with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{∬}_{D}z(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-z}z(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{2-z}(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[(4x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})]}_{x=0}^{x=2-z}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z(4(2-z)-\\frac{(2-z)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{16z}{3}-2{z}^{3}+\\frac{{z}^{4}}{3})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[\\frac{8{z}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{z}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{5}}{15}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}[\\frac{32}{3}-8+\\frac{32}{15}] \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
