    "q-161738": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161738",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}3x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}3x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3x[y]_{y=0}^{y=x}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3x(x-0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=2-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(16-12)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
