    "q-161772": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161772",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}xyz\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-2z},\\,0\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}xyz\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xyz\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xyz\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}xyz\\,dy]dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}xz{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}xz(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{x}^{3}z\\,dx\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{x}^{3}z\\,dx\\,dz & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-2z}}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(4-2z)^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\frac{1}{2}{[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(8-\\frac{32}{3}+4)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
