    "q-161751": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161751",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}20y\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[10{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1-x}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-x)^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-x)^{2}(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-2x+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-2x+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[10(x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
