    "q-161735": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161735",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x=1,$ and the line $z=x$ in the first quadrant.",
      "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}12y\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}12y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}6[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}6x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}6x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6x[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-161735-a",
