      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/3cba44923f4f583cf6e01ac87cdd6e5ca73a75993eef8322cd01bf44416f84f4.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/f112dd83a8cbb7563979dc170db23db7e178ba1762aca23fd4073c50e1c7a343.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5-x-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/71974fddc8e0e0b6a12fc6a248c15eea08c9f6b8a0823d50aede8aadc31a41fa.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5-x-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}4x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}4x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}4x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4x[y]_{y=0}^{y=5-x-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4x(5-x-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(20x-4{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(20x-4{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(20x-4{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[20xz-4{x}^{2}z-2x{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(32x-8{x}^{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(32x-8{x}^{2})\\,dx & ={[16{x}^{2}-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(64-\\frac{64}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{128}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
