      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/6f4bf1fe2f1a49f84b56702c4a83272c2f927ea4774eb677f43e525bf6cfb1f7.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}8x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/71f3fd0cbbde8adeca71688d6b53e2cd4cdf72076be3efa770cfebb8c10ffb76.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{z}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/cd84968e9e5300a18d087ba566202aba2b7166818a590cca03eac90d4f3f7a89.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{z}{2}\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}8x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/4-z/2}8x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/4-z/2}8x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/4-z/2}8x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}8x[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-3x/4-z/2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}8x(3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{z}{2})\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(24x-6{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(24x-6{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(24x-6{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[24xz-6{x}^{2}z-2x{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(72x-18{x}^{2}-18x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(54x-18{x}^{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(54x-18{x}^{2})\\,dx & ={[27{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(27-6)-0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
