    "q-161853": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161853",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/a1e4a1e39c85a037f3f4f49910b651300363ef34bee969464f5e711aa00986e3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/9165163be9ce95e7165f04d26e6ce8080699ab4d477eba3f804c849fdf1fb679.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/ca74bf149c1371fe9f1622586d9eb92fe180a9c9bb6a0c53d16f538b3c55f4a4.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z(4-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[8{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx & ={[12{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(12-0) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
