    "q-163509": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163509",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/335bf5e4e2a4ee9d0286eadb968e0e82c6afb18d47cd5258d6d1b6cee3d5c5a6.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}xz\\,\\text{d}V=$",
      "worked_solution": "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=1$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/b176bcf502a0801eae2bf470dfe4bf92852a34b06675fd74be78b30ccb4f6469.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14217845/assets/eb054b5f1567aa2c56842d79133fbbefc41a8b40730c688381d88e3ef06ccab7.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}xz\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}xz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}xz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}xz[y]_{y=1}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}2xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
